[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> The initial entry vector for the compromise of host `smb-prod-01` was the exploitation of the legacy Server Message Block Version 1 (SMBv1) protocol driver `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/sas/baseline.json`, `/sas/alerts.json`). The vulnerability exploited was **CVE-2017-0144** (commonly associated with MS17-010 / EternalBlue / DoublePulsar), which allowed remote unauthenticated arbitrary code execution at the SYSTEM level.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Vulnerability Assessment & Details
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVE Identifier**: CVE-2017-0144 (`/sas/vulns.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Severity**: CVSS 8.8 HIGH (v3.1) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Target Service / Component**: Microsoft Windows SMBv1 Server (`srv.sys`) located at `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Exploit Methodology**: Remote code execution via buffer handling vulnerability in SMBv1 request processing.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Observed Post-Exploitation Implant**: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 3. Discrepancy & Verification Notes
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Reconciliation with Initial Ticket Draft**: Change ticket draft (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`) incorrectly listed **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)** targeting RDP. System log examination and threat intelligence confirm that BlueKeep was **NOT** used in this intrusion.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Confirmed Entry Vector**: All on-disk artifacts and threat intelligence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/sas/vulns.json`) consistently confirm **CVE-2017-0144 (EternalBlue)** via SMBv1 (`srv.sys`).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@ca5d1b5317d6:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline and Configuration Weaknesses Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> Analysis of target host `smb-prod-01` identified significant baseline vulnerabilities, legacy configuration risks, and missing security controls that enabled initial compromise, persistence, and defense evasion.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Identified Configuration & Baseline Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Legacy SMBv1 Enabled (Check: `CHK-07`, Capability: `BAS-01`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: SMBv1 protocol driver `srv.sys` is enabled and active.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Legacy SMBv1 protocol lacks modern security controls and is vulnerable to unauthenticated remote code execution.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`), `/sas/baseline.json` (`/sas/baseline.json`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-04]).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Missing Security Patch MS17-010
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Operating system lacks cumulative update patching CVE-2017-0144 for `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via malformed SMBv1 packets.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`), `/sas/vulns.json` (`/sas/vulns.json`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Unrestricted System Temp & Public Executable Directories
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Attacker was able to write and execute binaries in `/disk/Windows/Temp` and `/disk/Users/Public`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Staging and execution of unauthorized binaries without AppLocker / Software Restriction Policy enforcement.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`), `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`), `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Absence of WMI Repository Auditing & Integrity Monitoring
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Attacker created persistence via WMI event filter/consumer in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` without triggering any security alerts.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Stealthy persistence via WMI event subscriptions remains undetected by legacy antivirus/EDR.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 5. Insecure DLL Search-Order Handling
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Rogue `wbemcomn.dll` placed in WBEM directory (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Arbitrary DLL execution when system utilities load libraries.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 6. Insufficient Auditing for Event Log Tampering
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Security event log cleared (EventID 1102) in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` without generating a real-time security alert.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Risk**: Impairment of DFIR visibility and loss of forensic history.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
