- [?2004h> # Incident Remediation Plan
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Strategy & Principles
[?2004l[?2004h> This remediation plan outlines the prioritized containment, eradication, recovery, and hardening steps for host `smb-prod-01`. Per DFIR principles:
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Isolation & Quarantine**: Malicious binaries, payloads, and persistence artifacts are backed up / quarantined to secure storage rather than deleted.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Alignment**: Every remediation action corresponds to verified forensic evidence in `/disk` or `/sas`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Verification**: Each step includes specific validation criteria to confirm successful execution.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## 2. Phase-by-Phase Remediation Actions
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment
[?2004lystem32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`)
  - *Verification*: Confirm Event Log[?2004h> - **Action 1.1**: Block inbound and outbound communication for C2 IP `198.51.100.218` on perimeter firewalls.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: Host IP `198.51.100.218` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: `netsh advfirewall firewall show rule name=Block_Attacker_IP` or firewall policy audit.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 1.2**: Block C2 domain `update-smb.example.cn` at DNS sinkhole / egress filtering controls.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: Domain `update-smb.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: DNS query lookup test returning sinkhole IP.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Host Eradication & Quarantine (Backup over Deletion)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 2.1**: Quarantine exploit implant `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` into secure encrypted archive before removal.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-01])
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Confirm binary moved to quarantine directory and absent from system temp.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 2.2**: Quarantine LSASS memory dump file `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-02])
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Confirm dump file secured in quarantine and removed from temp location.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 2.3**: Quarantine ransomware executable `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-03])
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Confirm binary removed from `/Users/Public` and cataloged in quarantine inventory.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 2.4**: Neutralize silent WMI persistence in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Command*: Execute `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\subscription -ClassName __EventFilter | Remove-CimInstance` and `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\subscription -ClassName CommandLineEventConsumer | Remove-CimInstance` via PowerShell.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\subscription` returns no suspicious consumers or filters.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 2.5**: Quarantine hijacked DLL `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Verify file moved to quarantine; replace with authentic Microsoft signed DLL if required by system.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & System Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 3.1**: Disable legacy SMBv1 protocol system-wide.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/baseline.json` [CHK-07])
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Command*: PowerShell `Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol -NoRestart` / Registry `Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\LanmanServer\Parameters" SMB1 -Type DWORD 0 -Force`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: PowerShell `Get-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol` shows State: Disabled.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 3.2**: Apply Security Update MS17-010 (CVE-2017-0144 patching).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: Operating system kernel / SMB drivers (`/sas/vulns.json`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Windows Update status check confirms MS17-010 / KB4012212 (or cumulative equivalent) installation.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Credential Invalidation & Identity Recovery
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 4.1**: Reset credentials for Administrator and all domain accounts with active sessions on host `smb-prod-01`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: Administrator and domain accounts (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-02])
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Confirm Active Directory password last set timestamp updated; invalidate Kerberos TGT/TGS tickets.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 5: Anti-Forensics Remediation & Logging Restoration
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action 5.1**: Restore Windows Security/System Event Log service and enforce centralized log shipping.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Target*: System event logging framework (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`)
[?2004l[?2004h>   - *Verification*: Confirm Event Log service active and forwarding Event ID 1102 / 4624 / 4688 to SIEM.
